{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless","id":986964,"title":"3 Legacies from Hapless","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T14:52:20-07:00","id":986964,"title":"3 Legacies from Hapless","content":"So...yeah for those of you have have viewed my other thread about picking a Legacy this is where I am, designing legacies. I have altered one Legacy the Scions of God, into Scions of Death. Instead of wanting to become angels these Moros want to become angels of death. Those sent to collect souls of the dead and safely usher them over to the other side. The second is an update of Stone Scribes (One I will need a lot of help on from someone who has done this sort of thing before), and the last is one I have thought of over time. White Reaper which is a left handed legacy that is viewed as wicked because they try to use their left handed methods for net good.<br /> <br /> Links to the Google Docs<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17jZ0Jg-fvoyW1MIy79ZswT8a56-5-fbJnj17DhdFA1A/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Scions of Death</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KR_xkuUOqaGwTCh0a707tq3QxU28n1ckpR4bSL3PQms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">White Reapers</a><br /> Stone Scribes<br /> <br /> All the feedback I can get is encouraged. Scions I don't know what to do for the 4th attainment or even if I did those right, and Stone Scribes, well I'll probably need help there as well, as I get to developing that one. I'll update this post with changes I've made either due to comments posted here or in the google docs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T05:16:24-07:00","id":987201,"title":"","content":"Hello. I've gotten some feedback on Scions of death and made some changes, as well as responded to some of the comments either asking for more help, highlighting a change made so that the helpful person may consider the change to see if it is helpful or makes things murky; or thanking for advice.<br /> Currently Scions of Death needs more help with the first attainment as I am suddenly thinking that it is just death based mage sight. So any helpful advice on ways to improve it or what would be a good change are appreciated.<br /> <br /> White Reapers<br /> Mostly done Death Scythes are getting a further work down, to include a new basic feature that will allow soul stones to be attached adding effective dots of arcana to rolls, and for calculating free reach. This will replace their Yantra bonus. 5th attainment needs a scythe bonus but I can't think of anything other than the scythe becomes sentient, able to heal it's self as long as not broken, and gaining some numia basically becoming a rank 2 familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:11:15-07:00","id":987241,"title":"","content":"I think your changes were improvements, overall. Scions has good bones for a legacy.<br /> You are, of course, welcome for the advice. 'Twas hopefully worth more than you paid for it.<br /> <br /> The most obvious first attainment is <i>Speak With the Dead</i> while wearing the mask.<br /> Alternately, though, Death Sight always on while wearing the mask (In essence, just reducing the Mana cost) works rather well. That allows it to automatically scale when the other attainment is learned at Death 2.<br /> <br /> By the book, a 1st attainment <i>Speak With the Dead</i> option would be either instant cast for basic duration in rounds or the donning of the mask becomes a preparatory ritual that lasts for a scene or two when you put it on (not instant casting since the single Reach goes into Advanced Duration) This leaves off the options for examining Fetters or talking to strange ghosts.This is annoying, since the 2nd dot of Death grants essentially all <i>but</i> those two options to Death Sight. of those two, then, I lean towards making Death Sight cheaper.<br /> <br /> My current favorite notion:<br /> <br /> It's obvious that the mask should count as a Yantra, regardless of any attainment, but there are a few things that could go extend that idea. The first attainment might simply allow the Scion to prepare the mask with appropriate magic and don it, rather than simply casting directly on himself. Only by wearing the mask would those spells have their effect, but the Duration and Potency of such effects are Advanced without need for Reach. These benefits supplement the simple Yantra bonus to the spell-casting roll itself. (possibly +2, possibly a bonus equal to the level of Attainment)<br /> <br /> With that take, the first attainment might not grant sight, per se, but it makes whatever magic is used a whole lot more useful. Wording of the attainment should describe the sorts of effects that can be enchanted into the mask in this way. Honestly, as long as the effects are personal and fit the reaper status, they should probably work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:35:16-07:00","id":987268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987241#post987241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, though, Death Sight always on while wearing the mask (In essence, just reducing the Mana cost) works rather well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the impression that using Active Mage Sight of a Ruling Arcanum doesn't cost Mana anyway. However, having it as an Attainment means it automatically succeeds, so it's a viable option either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:55:52-07:00","id":987279,"title":"","content":"Throwing ideas at the wall, but for Stone Scribes I'd probably make the 1st attainment function similarly to Soul Marks as it reveals the target's name Final or Momentary Name (Which isn't necessarily the same as their Sympathetic Name), and I'd let it work on corpses. The optional 2nd Attainment of Time could probably reveal their Sympathetic name like some kind of hyper fast and specific Postcognition. Alternatively the Time part could be what allows the Death part to work on corpses.The 2nd attainment could be Decay, Stone Scribes use it specifically to carve a true name into stone tablets, but obviously it has other uses as well. The optional with Time 2 could be something like fixing the carved name in place as a Representational Yantra regardless of the passage of more time or changes to the owner of the name. You could make it temporary with the living and permanent with the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:29:32-07:00","id":987306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987268#post987268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the impression that using Active Mage Sight of a Ruling Arcanum doesn't cost Mana anyway. However, having it as an Attainment means it automatically succeeds, so it's a viable option either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still getting familiar with 2e. Can you tell? You're completely right. Plain as day at the top of p.91.<br /> I'm pretty convinced making the mask a sort-of super Rune Yantra for appropriate magic solves a lot of issues at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the gist of what you're throwing down, Mrmdubois.<br /> <br /> I would <i>certainly</i> require the Time component to get the name out of a corpse, given that they focus so heavily on studying the final moments. Just protects that theme.<br /> <br /> The name should be a representational Yantra for Time and Space, but the temporal sympathy should degrade over time pretty much using the normal Time rules on the matter, except if the subject dies. A Final Name would be truly permanent.<br /> <br /> Not sold on Decay for carving and such. I really lean towards the Scribe just scribing.<br /> <br /> I should dig out the book and reread their original write-up. (anyone recall which one are the scribes in?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:32:36-07:00","id":987308,"title":"","content":"They're in Legacies the Sublime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T10:07:33-07:00","id":987321,"title":"","content":"All right, I think I got scions pretty well covered. Anyone have any hints on white reapers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:25:47-07:00","id":987404,"title":"","content":"White Reapers are a bit intimidating crunch-wise. By giving them ways to reduce Arcana costs and by introducing a new mechanic you've strayed far off the beaten path. They kind of resemble the Timori Legacy, which was also an odd duck. I think people find it hard to recommend anything without falling back on the standard Legacy rules and they don't want to diss your ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:10:38-07:00","id":987431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987404#post987404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Reapers are a bit intimidating crunch-wise. By giving them ways to reduce Arcana costs and by introducing a new mechanic you've strayed far off the beaten path. They kind of resemble the Timori Legacy, which was also an odd duck. I think people find it hard to recommend anything without falling back on the standard Legacy rules and they don't want to diss your ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got that idea from page 238 Second paragraph. Where it talks about consuming and gaining aspects of magic from it. I tried to work that in. Though the &quot;That's a bit too powerful man&quot; is constructive criticism, and I happily accept that.<br /> <br /> Maybe raise the min Experience cost with stone expenditure to 2? Or have them give 1 arcane beat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 10-14-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:50:31-07:00","id":987454,"title":"","content":"If you want to keep the Legacy rules-compliant, take note of the excerpt below. Note that you don't have to. You can twist the rules into a pretzel for personal use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 238</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reapers do not have any special mechanics beyond that \u2014 their Left-Handed nature comes from their use of a power available to many mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shortcuts to power found through Reaping are more of a fluff matter. When it comes to crunch, no Arcana discounts or extra Beats are necessary. All Mages gain Arcane Beats for learning new stuff. According to existing rules, the Reaper can gain Beats with each dissected Soul - no tweaks necessary. This addresses my main concern.<br /> <br /> Secondly, did you consider what the Legacy used to be before the Marguerite reformed it? The two branches probably have at least the first Attainment in common. While we're at it, the Legacy comes with an in-built antagonist faction, so that's a great plus. Oddly, none of the Attainments allow soul theft. Instead, you sneak in an extra Attainment by having the Scythe create Soul Stones. That's my only gripe, since Scythes themselves are very flavorful and a good fit for the Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T15:57:59-07:00","id":987476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987454#post987454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to keep the Legacy rules-compliant, take note of the excerpt below. Note that you don't have to. You can twist the rules into a pretzel for personal use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Shortcuts to power found through Reaping are more of a fluff matter. When it comes to crunch, no Arcana discounts or extra Beats are necessary. All Mages gain Arcane Beats for learning new stuff. According to existing rules, the Reaper can gain Beats with each dissected Soul - no tweaks necessary. This addresses my main concern.<br /> <br /> Secondly, did you consider what the Legacy used to be before the Marguerite reformed it? The two branches probably have at least the first Attainment in common. While we're at it, the Legacy comes with an in-built antagonist faction, so that's a great plus. Oddly, none of the Attainments allow soul theft. Instead, you sneak in an extra Attainment by having the Scythe create Soul Stones. That's my only gripe, since Scythes themselves are very flavorful and a good fit for the Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were the Black Reapers before [Wow I suck at naming stuff], and both do share the same first Legacy and a love for soul harvesting scythes. The only difference is the black reapers first attainment wasn't centered around detecting other supernaturals but instead finding sleepers and other mages with interesting souls to examine.<br /> <br /> Though you are right in that I did kind of slip that in there, the scythe is just too iconic not to. Maybe I'll give them an extra persistent mental condition to offset that benefit? Or some other malus? After some feedback I did another revision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 10-14-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:36:50-07:00","id":987626,"title":"","content":"I'd probably make the Scythe its own attainment, honestly. Say, <i>Ectoplasmic Shaping</i> that can form a sickle or scythe. That's simple enough to do. <br /> <br /> I could see Scythe upgrades as the purview and work of optional attainments. With the Scythe as the focus, I might even play around with multiple optional arcana sources. Matter to make it truly physical. Fate to let it sever bonds. That sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:22:40-07:00","id":987671,"title":"","content":"As asked, I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987669-%E2%80%8B-2e-fan-stone-scribes\">Stone Scribes 2E update</a>. More I do those, less time it take me - this ones I made in less than 2 hours. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:30:55-07:00","id":987672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987476#post987476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'll give them an extra persistent mental condition to offset that benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. The trick is in finding something that will hinder the character, but won't cripple them. What if you make the Scythe non-replaceable? Losing it becomes a big deal, and the Reaper is denied their Legacy Attainments until they get it back. If it gets destroyed, then it can be replaced (let's not get sadistic). This way it would resemble, or could even be a Soul Stone.<br /> <br /> I thought about making the Scythe simply an Imbued Item. Consider this: The Scythe holds a Death 5 effect, for stealing souls on non-humans. If made a standard Attainment, your character will gain that ability at Gnosis 8! That's way too late. However, a Mage and their Master can craft a Scythe together. The Master casts the &quot;Soul Jar&quot; and &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; spells. This gives us some Mentor-Student bonding and makes losing the Scythe a big deal. Paying for the Scythe with Merit dots makes it balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:25:00-07:00","id":987760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987672#post987672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a bad idea. The trick is in finding something that will hinder the character, but won't cripple them. What if you make the Scythe non-replaceable? Losing it becomes a big deal, and the Reaper is denied their Legacy Attainments until they get it back. If it gets destroyed, then it can be replaced (let's not get sadistic). This way it would resemble, or could even be a Soul Stone.<br /> <br /> I thought about making the Scythe simply an Imbued Item. Consider this: The Scythe holds a Death 5 effect, for stealing souls on non-humans. If made a standard Attainment, your character will gain that ability at Gnosis 8! That's way too late. However, a Mage and their Master can craft a Scythe together. The Master casts the &quot;Soul Jar&quot; and &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; spells. This gives us some Mentor-Student bonding and makes losing the Scythe a big deal. Paying for the Scythe with Merit dots makes it balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it! I'll make that change! I'll go back and see exactly what the costs for Imbued items are and add the part about legacy atainments cannot be used until they get their scythe back. Wait would it be enhaced or imbued?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:25:37-07:00","id":987884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987760#post987760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it! I'll make that change! I'll go back and see exactly what the costs for Imbued items are and add the part about legacy atainments cannot be used until they get their scythe back. Wait would it be enhaced or imbued?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be Imbued, because it allows you to cast a spell. That spell would be &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; with Touch Range and Reach spent on Instant Casting. If I understand the rules correctly (and they're vague on some points), adding more Reach would cause a Paradox risk, so it should be avoided. That would be a five-dot item, but you might want to increase its Mana capacity. Note that you need to cast &quot;Soul Jar&quot; on your own before using the item, but that can be done even by a beginning Reaper.<br /> <br /> If you're making the Scythe an Imbued item, I would do the following: Make &quot;Soul Jar&quot; and &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; two of the Legacy's Attainments. The Scythe would be a crutch that the Reaper needs until reaching Gnosis 8 or Death 5. I wouldn't make their Attainments dependent on the Scythe. It's not really connected to the Reaper's soul, and losing it makes them unable to harvest anything on their own until late in their career.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:44:30-07:00","id":987946,"title":"","content":"Buy why cast sever the awakened soul each time when you can just have it be an enhanced item, and the spell is permanently cast into the weapon, with a duration of indefinite? Same with Soul Jar, it just lasts forever. But one more thought. Sever the awakened soul removes that soul while the subject is still living. The death scythe as I designed it removes the soul upon death, when it would normally comes lose anyway. In short Sever the Awakened soul isn't needed, more like harvest the awakened soul. That soul is already free of it's body, I'm just pulling it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:26:05-07:00","id":987960,"title":"","content":"<i>Sever the Awakened Soul</i> is lasting, so boosting it's duration up to indefinite makes it repeat at your casting interval... (I think that still applies to Imbued Items) which would normally do what you want, but not always. To get an Item that cuts souls whenever swung, imbuing that as its trigger is the obvious way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:40:19-07:00","id":987965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987946#post987946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buy why cast sever the awakened soul each time when you can just have it be an enhanced item, and the spell is permanently cast into the weapon, with a duration of indefinite? Same with Soul Jar, it just lasts forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that if you store &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; in an object it becomes an Imbued Item, not an Enhanced Item, and it's cast as needed. Can Imbued Items store spells that are constantly on? That's a good question, actually. Please, consider asking here:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition\">Ask a simple question, Awakened edition</a><br /> <br /> The Scythe could be made into a permanent &quot;Soul Jar&quot;, just as you say. However, that would mean you only have a single one, and can't store a collection of souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987946#post987946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But one more thought. Sever the awakened soul removes that soul while the subject is still living. The death scythe as I designed it removes the soul upon death, when it would normally comes lose anyway. In short Sever the Awakened soul isn't needed, more like harvest the awakened soul. That soul is already free of it's body, I'm just pulling it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, upon death souls pass on to wherever they go. They don't linger, ready to be harvested. The spell needs to pull the soul out of its natural cycle. It's effectively &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot;, only with narrower circumstances of use.<br /> <br /> I feel like I distracted you from your goal. If so, sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:50:19-07:00","id":987971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986964-3-legacies-from-hapless?p=987960#post987960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Sever the Awakened Soul</i> is lasting, so boosting it's duration up to indefinite makes it repeat at your casting interval... (I think that still applies to Imbued Items) which would normally do what you want, but not always. To get an Item that cuts souls whenever swung, imbuing that as its trigger is the obvious way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can't be right. &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; has a duration. If it times out, the soul should return to its owner, unless it's stored in a Soul Jar. That's how &quot;Sever Soul&quot; does it. If you make &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; Indefinite, the soul will just float in Twilight until something happens to it. Also, Imbued Items are Lasting, but spells inside them don't have to be.<br /> <br /> I'm using the advance pdf and the errata. Maybe that's the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:50:40-07:00","id":988159,"title":"","content":"Editionitis. Dang, it really <i>isn't</i> Lasting. Man, they defanged it right proper.<br /> On the other hand, they let you Thrall someone with it, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T07:16:34-07:00","id":988238,"title":"","content":"They didn't defang it, they just made it a two step process, sever the soul, plunk it in a magic jar. Combine cast and it can still be a one step permanent process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:24:39-07:00","id":988396,"title":"","content":"Yeah, really they did. It was <i>always</i> a two step process to <i>stash</i> it. Previously, it was a one step slow-kill. Now, it recovers itself over time.<br /> Previously, fixing soul loss <i>required</i> a mage with Spirit. Now, time or, at very worst, a mage with enough Death or Prime to dispel the mess.<br /> <br /> Life got meaner in 2e, but soul loss got much softer. That's fine, given that they rather thoroughly redefined what a soul <i>is</i>, while they were at it, but there isn't any way this constitutes the same level of risk when there are some many easier ways to recover.<br /> <br /> The only counterargument I'm seeing is that the spell to swipe the soul seems a lot easier, only being Withstood by Resolve and not having quite so many layers of protection available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-16-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}